 au.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123138Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creation and Production: Contemporary Music
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's creation and production grant for contemporary m
 usic supports the creation and production of new musical works\, including
  commissioned compositions\, music theatre\, sound installations\, and con
 temporary productions. Open to nationally established music professionals 
 and ensembles from Switzerland working in contemporary music\, music theat
 re\, sound art\, or contemporary folk music\, with prior Pro Helvetia supp
 ort. ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\
 , or permanent residency with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; 
 not open to practitioners without a Swiss connection. AMOUNT: maximum CHF 
 25\,000\, depending on overall project size. Deadlines twice a year: 1 Mar
 ch (23:59 CET) and 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia po
 rtal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Nation
 ally established Switzerland-based professionals and ensembles in contempo
 rary music\, music theatre\, sound art\, or contemporary folk.\nAward: Max
 imum CHF 25\,000 (depending on overall project size). No application fee.\
 nDuration: Creation/production of new works\; deadlines twice yearly (1 Ma
 rch and 1 September).\n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/crea
 tion-and-production-contemporary-music?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/creation-and-production-contempo
 rary-music?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nationally established Switzerland-based professionals and ensembl
 es in contemporary music\, music theatre\, sound art\, or contemporary fol
 k.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-new-production-performing-arts-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123138Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: New Production (Performing Arts)
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's new production grant funds new performing arts p
 roductions\, including digital and hybrid formats\, by Switzerland-based a
 rtists and companies with confirmed venue bookings and co-financing in pla
 ce. Open to Swiss citizens\, permanent residents active in Switzerland\, o
 r independent groups and cultural institutions based in Switzerland. ELIGI
 BILITY: requires a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or perma
 nent residency with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open t
 o practitioners without a Swiss connection. The grant amount is not specif
 ied on the call page and depends on the project. Deadlines twice a year: 1
  March (23:59 CET) and 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helveti
 a portal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Sw
 itzerland-based independent performing arts companies and artists.\nAward:
  Amount not specified on the call page. No application fee.\nDuration: New
  performing arts production with confirmed venue bookings and co-financing
 \; deadlines twice yearly (1 March and 1 September).\n\nMore: https://proh
 elvetia.ch/en/find-support/new-production?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/new-production?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based independent performing arts companies and artist
 s.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-focus-photo-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123138Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Focus Photo (Visual Arts)
DESCRIPTION:Focus Photo is a Pro Helvetia grant supporting new production i
 n artistic\, documentary or applied photography\; projects may be based on
  analogue\, digital or post-photographic image practices. FOR WHOM: cross-
 regionally established photographers and artists. Pro Helvetia's general r
 equirements apply\, meaning a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship
 \, or permanent residency with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\;
  Swiss-based groups and collectives may also apply. SELECTION CRITERIA: a 
 high degree of artistic originality and quality\; feasibility of the proje
 ct\; and the importance of the work for the applicant's artistic developme
 nt. Applications are assessed by a jury under Pro Helvetia's general decis
 ion-making process. AMOUNT: maximum CHF 25\,000. WHAT TO SUBMIT: a descrip
 tion of the planned project\, an implementation plan and a budget with fin
 ancial plan (including all financial assistance requested from third parti
 es) in a single PDF\; a portfolio documenting work over the last three yea
 rs (including links to videos\, maximum 20 pages)\; a CV including previou
 s exhibition activities in a single PDF\; and\, if the project is planned 
 as part of an exhibition\, an invitation letter from the organiser confirm
 ing the planned presentation. EXCLUDED: projects involving journalistic re
 search and reporting (with publication in print or digital media) and PR p
 rojects\; new editions\, commissioned works and projects that are part of 
 an advertising campaign\; and photographic publications. ONE APPLICATION R
 ULE: across production grants\, production grants with presentation\, Focu
 s Photo and Perform!\, only one application may be submitted per person or
  collective per calendar year\, whichever format you choose\; recipients o
 f production grants may only reapply for one of these formats once the pro
 ject is complete. KEY DATES: applications open 1 July\; submission deadlin
 e 1 September\, 23:59 CEST\; notification of decision within four months\;
  earliest project start 1 January. Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nO
 rganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-base
 d photographers and collectives.\nAward: Maximum grant of CHF 25\,000 towa
 rd the production. No application fee.\nDuration: New photography producti
 on\; applications open 1 July\, deadline 1 September\, decision within fou
 r months\, earliest project start 1 January\n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.c
 h/en/find-support/focus-photo?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/focus-photo?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based photographers and collectives.
END:VEVENT
